<section class="section">
  <h2>What it does</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">
    Self-hosted apps each want their own login. Heautou lets them all use one
    sign-in, without running Keycloak or Authentik: one container, one folder of
    data, and a web page for adding the apps and the people who use them.
  </p>

  <ul class="card-grid">
    <li>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>One sign-in for every app</h3>
        <p>A standard OIDC provider for the authorization code flow, with client secrets or PKCE; apps can pair themselves from a setup link.</p>
      </article>
    </li>
    <li>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Two-factor and passkeys</h3>
        <p>Users add an authenticator app or passkeys on their account page, and apps can see from the token how they signed in.</p>
      </article>
    </li>
    <li>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>No database server needed</h3>
        <p>Everything is kept in a database built into heautou, or in your own Postgres if you have one. Secrets are sealed under a key you choose, and every sign-in and change goes in an audit log.</p>
      </article>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="section" id="start">
  <h2>Get started</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <pre class="code"><code>docker run -d -p 3000:3000 -v heautou-data:/data \
  -e ISSUER_URL=http://localhost:3000/oidc \
  ghcr.io/cubicecho/heautou:latest

# then open http://localhost:3000 and create the first admin</code></pre>
  </div>

